                <li>11 open-source Cowork plugins at launch across functions like Sales, Legal, Finance, and Marketing.</li>
                <li>Plugins bundle skills, connectors, slash commands, and sub-agents into one download.</li>
                <li>Plugins are currently saved locally; org-wide sharing is planned.</li>
              </ul>
              <h5 class="text-xs font-bold text-red-300 uppercase tracking-wide">🛡️ Operational Considerations (Documented)</h5>
              <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2">
                <li><strong>Local storage today:</strong> Plugins are saved locally; Anthropic says org-wide sharing is coming.</li>
                <li><strong>Review limits:</strong> Basic automated review for submissions; “Anthropic Verified” gets additional review, with stated limits.</li>
                <li><strong>Trust burden:</strong> Anthropic advises installing only plugins from developers you trust.</li>
              </ol>
              <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">Public-sector note: reporting says the DoD designated Anthropic a “supply-chain risk” and advised contractors to avoid commercial activity, while Anthropic disputes the designation and its legal standing.</p>
              <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-red-200 font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide">Prescriptive answer: position centralized governance and admin control as the differentiator.</p>
              <h5 class="text-xs font-bold text-emerald-300 uppercase tracking-wide">💡 Battlecards: Handling Claude Plugin Objections</h5>
              <p><strong>Objection 1:</strong> "Claude’s Cowork Plugins give us a pre-built legal and HR department." <br />
              <strong>Rebuttal:</strong> Agent Builder provides a visual workflow canvas, and Connector Registry centralizes integrations under admin control.</p>
              <p><strong>Objection 2:</strong> "Developers prefer Claude Code plugins." <br />
              <strong>Rebuttal:</strong> OpenAI’s AgentKit emphasizes governed workflows plus guardrails for input/output checks.</p>
              <p><strong>Objection 3:</strong> "MCP is the standard." <br />
              <strong>Rebuttal:</strong> OpenAI positions guardrails and a Connector Registry gated by Global Admin Console for governance.</p>
              <h5 class="text-xs font-bold text-yellow-300 uppercase tracking-wide">🚀 The Bottom Line</h5>
              <p>Claude Plugins are packaged skills + connectors. OpenAI positions a governed agent OS with Agent Builder, Connector Registry, and guardrails.</p>
              <p class="font-semibold text-white">— OpenAI GTM Strategy Team</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">Sources: <a class="underline hover:text-gray-300" href="https://claude.com/blog/cowork-plugins" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Claude Cowork plugins</a> · <a class="underline hover:text-gray-300" href="https://claude.com/plugins" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Claude plugins FAQ</a> · <a class="underline hover:text-gray-300" href="https://www.vktr.com/ai-news/openai-launches-agentkit-to-streamline-ai-agent-development/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">VKTR AgentKit</a> · <a class="underline hover:text-gray-300" href="https://www.nudgesecurity.com/post/openai-agentkit-and-agent-builder-building-secure-ai-agents" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Nudge Security</a> · <a class="underline hover:text-gray-300" href="https://openai.github.io/openai-agents-python/guardrails/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenAI Guardrails</a> · <a class="underline hover:text-gray-300" href="https://www.cbsnews.com/news/hegseth-declares-anthropic-supply-chain-risk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CBS News</a> · <a class="underline hover:text-gray-300" href="https://www.wired.com/story/anthropic-supply-chain-risk-shockwaves-silicon-valley/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WIRED</a> · <a class="underline hover:text-gray-300" href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/02/tech-workers-urge-dod-congress-to-withdraw-anthropic-label-as-a-supply-chain-risk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TechCrunch</a></p>
